736 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 259 0 R
/E (This study presents a comparative Machine Learning and Deep Learning framework for predicting the reconstruction quality of Helicobacter pylori virulence genes from genome assemblies. Random Forest, XGBoost, CNN, and BiLSTM models were evaluated for classifying gene sequences into complete, fragmented, and incomplete categories. Among the individual models, XGBoost achieved the best performance, while a stacking ensemble further improved classification accuracy. SHAP-based explainability analysis identified internal stop codons as the most influential biological feature, demonstrating the potential of automated AI-driven approaches for reliable virulence gene reconstruction assessment.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
